/use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"39\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-39\"></use><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g><rect width=\"1260.7\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>We want every pair drawn to have <b>one blue</b> and <b>one green</b>. Since there are 6 blue and 6 green balls, we will draw a total of 6 pairs.</p>\n<p>For each pair to be mixed (one of each colour), we must match the 6 blue balls with the 6 green balls in pairs. The number of such “good” pairings is counted by choosing and matching one ball of one colour with one ball of the other colour.</p>\n<p>The total number of ways to split 12 balls into 6 pairs (without caring about the order of drawing inside a pair) is counted separately. The required probability is:</p>\n<p>Probability <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -4.436ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"19.836ex\" height=\"6.805ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1047.1 8767.3 3007.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(1055.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(1496.1,516.8) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"230A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-230A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(444,0)\"><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(944,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g da